    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0111" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>President Roosevelt to Prime Minister Churchill<anchor n="1" xml:id="d44-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-01-06">6 January 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 692, Personal and Top Secret, from the President for the Prime
                    Minister.</p>
                <p>Your 874 and 875. I am informed by Harriman that U. J. will meet us at Yalta
                    February first or second.</p>
                <p>Preparations are being made to take care of us and our Staff in undamaged houses
                    in Yalta. I will send my ship to Sevastopol to arrive three or four days in
                    advance of my arrival.</p>
                <p>There is a chance that weather might permit of the ship’s anchoring off the place
                    of meeting.</p>
                <p>With favorable weather at sea I can arrive Malta February second, and it is
                    necessary to proceed by air the same day in order to keep the date with U.
                    J.</p>
                <p>That is why I regret that in view of the time available to me for this journey it
                    will not be possible for us to meet your suggestion and have a British-American
                    Staff meeting at Malta before proceeding to <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Argonaut</hi>. I do not think that by not having a meeting at Malta any
                    time will be lost at <hi rendition="#small-caps">Argonaut</hi>.</p>
                <p>I am envious of your visits to the great battlefront which are denied to me by
                    distance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d44-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d44-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
